---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
import ToolVote from '../../../components/ToolVote.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Cutover Control Center"
  description="Hundreds of moving parts, and a plan that can start anywhere — typed in here or dropped in from a spreadsheet. It answers what is running, what is late and who is waiting. Working prototype."
>
  <main class="reading" id="main">
    <section class="block insight-page">
      <p class="kicker"><a href="/tools/">Tools</a></p>
      <h1>Cutover Control Center</h1>

      <p class="lede">
        A large migration has hundreds of moving parts, and the plan usually lives in a spreadsheet. Fair
        enough — that is where plans get written, argued over and pasted around. What a spreadsheet cannot do
        is answer, at three in the morning, what is running right now, what is late, and who is waiting for
        whom.
      </p>

      <p>
        So the plan can start anywhere. Build it here and drop an export on top later, or import first and add
        the rest by hand — it is a simple interface on top of a simple database, and that alone takes a
        surprising amount of friction out of a cutover weekend.
      </p>

      <h2>What it does</h2>

      <ul class="feature-list">
        <li>
          <strong>Start with an empty screen.</strong> One button makes the first activity and opens it; after
          that you type a name, press Enter, and keep going. Quick entry inherits the filters you are looking
          through, so narrow to one system and one stream and what you type lands there. Duplicate gives the
          next one its starting point — the run-book and the criteria come along, the status, the actual times,
          the blocking and the comments do not. Delete says what depends on the activity before it goes.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Or drop the spreadsheet in.</strong> Excel, CSV or a Google Sheet: map the columns once, and
          add as many as you like — a master document, a run-book, one system's own view. What you built by
          hand collects under a source called <em>Built in the tool</em> and filters, groups and merges exactly
          like an imported one, so the order is free in both directions. Nothing is merged or linked
          automatically unless the identifiers matched exactly; where they did not, it proposes a relationship
          and waits for you to confirm or reject it.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The questions a spreadsheet cannot answer.</strong> Running now, starting soon, late,
          blocked, critical at risk — as counts you can press, on one screen, against a clock. A blocked line
          says who it is waiting for rather than that it is red.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Several ways into the same plan.</strong> A timeline, a dependency graph, the run-book, the
          teams, and an execution view built for the night itself: bigger type, fewer things, the next
          milestone and how far off it is.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>The prototype</h2>

      <p>
        Loaded with an example cutover — 444 activities from three files, and a clock you can move.
      </p>

      <p class="demo-open">
        <a class="demo-button" href="/tools/cutover-app.html">Open the clickable prototype →</a>
        <span class="demo-hint">It is an application. A big screen suits it.</span>
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="demo-wide">
      <iframe
        id="cutover-demo"
        src="/tools/cutover-app.html"
        title="Cutover Control Center prototype"
        loading="lazy"
      ></iframe>
      <p class="demo-fallback">
        <a href="/tools/cutover-app.html">Open the prototype full-screen</a>
      </p>
      <p class="demo-narrow">
        The prototype is a control room and wants a wider screen than this one.
        <a href="/tools/cutover-app.html">Open it</a> on something larger.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="block insight-page">
      <h2>Where it is</h2>

      <p>
        A working prototype with a bundled example plan, and no server behind it — everything you do stays in
        the browser. If you run cutovers and want to try it against a real plan,
        <a href="/contact/">write to me</a>.
      </p>

      <ToolVote tool="cutover" />
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .insight-page h2 {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    margin: 2.6rem 0 0.7rem;
  }
  .feature-list {
    margin: 1.4rem 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
  }
  .feature-list li {
    margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
  }
  .feature-list strong {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .demo-open {
    margin: 1.6rem 0 0;
  }
  .demo-hint {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-left: 0.8rem;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--bark);
  }
  @media (max-width: 30rem) {
    .demo-hint {
      display: block;
      margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
    }
  }
  .demo-button {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.6rem 1.1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--moss);
    border-radius: 2px;
    font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--moss);
    transition: background 0.15s ease, color 0.15s ease;
  }
  .demo-button:hover {
    background: var(--moss);
    color: var(--paper);
  }
  /* A control room wants a viewport of its own, so it steps out of the reading
     column and keeps a fixed one. */
  .demo-wide {
    width: min(65rem, calc(100vw - 3rem));
    margin: 2rem 0 3.4rem 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
  }
  .demo-wide iframe {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: min(46rem, 82vh);
    border: 1px solid var(--mist);
    border-radius: 2px;
    background: var(--card);
  }
  .demo-fallback {
    margin: 0.6rem 0 0;
    font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .demo-narrow {
    display: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0 1.5rem;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--bark);
  }
  /* Below this the panels stack into a column and stop being a control room. */
  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .demo-wide {
      width: 100vw;
    }
    .demo-wide iframe,
    .demo-fallback {
      display: none;
    }
    .demo-narrow {
      display: block;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Same-origin, so the site's theme toggle can be handed through to the frame.
  const frame = document.getElementById('cutover-demo') as HTMLIFrameElement | null;

  if (frame) {
    const syncTheme = () => {
      const doc = frame.contentDocument;
      if (!doc) return;
      const theme = document.documentElement.dataset.theme;
      if (theme) doc.documentElement.dataset.theme = theme;
      else delete doc.documentElement.dataset.theme;
    };

    frame.addEventListener('load', syncTheme);
    if (frame.contentDocument?.readyState === 'complete') syncTheme();

    new MutationObserver(syncTheme).observe(document.documentElement, {
      attributes: true,
      attributeFilter: ['data-theme'],
    });
  }
</script>
